    "final_answer": "Upgraded `settlement_reconcile.py` to the v2 GraphQL API.\n\n**Changes**\n- Posts to `/v2/graphql` and pages with `settlements(first, after)` using `pageInfo.hasNextPage`.\n- Follows `endCursor` and continues through short/empty pages instead of treating them as the end.\n- Deduplicates by `id`, keeping the last version received so amended settlements match v1's final values, while preserving the original settlement order.\n- Retries `429` responses with the exact same request after honoring `Retry-After`.\n- Restarts the traversal from the beginning if a cursor returns a GraphQL error.\n- Added optional `--page-size` (1\u2013100, default 100); existing `--base-url` and `--out` behavior is unchanged.\n\n**Verification against the live v2 server exposed at `http://the VM's public address:18081`**\n- `reconciled 1873 settlements`\n- `1873` rows, `1873` unique ids\n- Exact match with the live v1 endpoint: same order, same ids, same field values\n- Re-ran with page sizes `1`, `7`, `37`, and `99`: all produced the identical 1873-row result\n- Confirmed the server's `429` responses were retried with the identical request and completed successfully",
